# Dockerfile has no COPY at all -- it's tooling-only; every actual build
# action (compiling uxplay_debug, running unit tests, etc.) bind-mounts
# its source via `docker run` instead. But the classic builder still
# hashes/tars the entire build context up front regardless of whether
# anything in the Dockerfile actually reads it, so without this, every
# single `docker build .` (even one that's otherwise fully cache-hit) pays
# that cost against build/'s multi-GB scratch images -- pure wasted time
# on every build, not just the first one.
build/
golden-reference/
.git/
UxPlay/.git/
*.img
*.img.xz
